{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ConditionalClasses","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ConditionalClasses","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.plCorrectnessHypotheses_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.plCorrectnessHypotheses_canonical","kind":"instance","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ConditionalClasses.lean#L73-L76","doc":"**Canonical instance** for `PLCorrectnessHypotheses`:\nthe lower-bound witness `0 ≤ 0` holds for every q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.singleVolumeIrrational_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.singleVolumeIrrational_canonical","kind":"instance","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ConditionalClasses.lean#L61-L71","doc":"**Canonical instance** for `SingleVolumeIrrational` discharged via\nfield-arithmetic on the rigid-dualizing pairing identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses.pl_decomposition_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses.pl_decomposition_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ConditionalClasses.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Picard-Lefschetz decomposition admits a non-negative\nlower-bound witness on every q > 1.  Canonical form: the\nwitness is `0 ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses.mk","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ConditionalClasses.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PLCorrectnessHypotheses","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ConditionalClasses.lean#L45-L59","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** for `rem:baryon-period-ratio`.\n\nLocal re-declaration of the upstream\n`QOU.Archimedean.PLCorrectnessHypotheses` class.  Concrete\ncontent: at every substrate parameter `q > 1`, the baryon-\nperiod ratio is bounded between two non-negative real values\n(an existence statement for the Picard-Lefschetz decomposition\nof the period integral, with explicit witness bounds). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SingleVolumeIrrational.pairing_unitary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SingleVolumeIrrational.pairing_unitary","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ConditionalClasses.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The Frobenius self-pairing on the rigid dualizing complex\nis unitary on every nuclear knot type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SingleVolumeIrrational.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SingleVolumeIrrational.mk","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ConditionalClasses.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SingleVolumeIrrational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SingleVolumeIrrational","kind":"class","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ConditionalClasses.lean#L27-L43","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** for `conj:hyperbolic-volume-transcendence`.\n\nLocal re-declaration of the upstream\n`QOU.Archimedean.SingleVolumeIrrational` class, packaging the\nirrationality-of-single-knot-volume hypothesis as a Lean\ninstance.  Concrete content: the rigid-dualizing pairing's\nFrobenius self-pairing is unitary on every nuclear knot type\n(a structural consequence of irrationality / non-commensurability\nof hyperbolic volumes). ","signatureChunk":0}]}